 #edb/ref 17592186436797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436810 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436810 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436810 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436810 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a02475ca-ca51-5bbb-9fb2-8ed70c95ef71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436811 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cb2a33dc-019b-539c-8057-1ac05dffb007" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436812 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ef5c36a4-d082-5926-820f-4cd3513e1032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1071 "Let  $E=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436813 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-15$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-15{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436814 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}=7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75075" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436815 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-8$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42809" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e584c32-a3dd-5eaa-a4dc-b23f04848d16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436816 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1069 "q-31977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436817 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix  multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83a65485-4098-56b8-8fd5-9fb601be0cb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436818 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88681796-21e9-5e72-a195-e1da66276721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436819 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-6$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436820 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $5$ times the second row: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75088" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436821 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436822 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$  \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
